OpenSSL 3.5.9 is an external build dependency, downloaded separately under the
Apache License 2.0. Its source archive and license are not embedded in this QBTC
source delivery. Upstream: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/tree/openssl-3.5.9

External Wycheproof verification data is read from the pinned OpenSSL source
archive; that file carries the OpenSSL Apache 2.0 notice and identifies the
upstream Wycheproof commit. No private keys from external fixtures are copied
into QBTC. No external cryptographic algorithm source is reimplemented here.

cryptography==50.0.2 is an optional test-only dependency, not a runtime dependency
of QBTC executables. The cross-check is between OpenSSL-backed interfaces, not
between independently designed cryptographic implementations.

QBTC Windows previews include cross-compiled x64 executables under app/bin/.
They statically link OpenSSL and toolchain runtime components. Upstream license
texts are included under app/licenses/ (licenses/ in the source delivery).
Executables are unsigned; current preview changes still require native Windows
verification. The OpenSSL source archive is not embedded. Full toolchain and
independent dependency audit remain outstanding.
